-- Singapore Penal Code 1871 - Chapter 18, the "Currency and bank notes" part:
-- ss 489A-489I. (The forgery part, ss 463-477A, is in
-- pc-documents-defamation-forgery.l4.)
--
--   s 489A  forging or counterfeiting currency or bank notes; (2) defines
--           "bank note", "coin", "currency" for ss 489A-489I
--   s 489B  using as genuine, trafficking in, forged or counterfeit currency
--   s 489C  possessing forged or counterfeit currency
--   s 489D  instruments or materials for forging or counterfeiting currency
--   s 489E  abetting in Singapore counterfeiting of currency out of Singapore
--   s 489F  diminishing the weight or altering the composition of a coin
--   s 489G  altering the appearance of currency
--   s 489H  delivering altered currency
--   s 489I  possessing altered currency
--
-- Source: Penal Code 1871, 2020 Revised Edition, SSO "Current version as at
-- 09 Sep 2026" (inputs/PC1871.txt), page footers removed.
--
-- One facts record, `Currency Facts`, for the whole part: the offences share
-- their object (currency or a bank note) and most of their fault elements.
-- The s 489A(2) definitions are a drill-down over their own atoms
-- (`Currency Description Facts`); the offence ladders read "currency or bank
-- note" as one flat leaf (notes/PLAN.md §3.3).

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `pc-domain`
IMPORT `pc-general`
IMPORT `pc-documents-defamation-common`

§ `Penal Code 1871 - Chapter 18, currency and bank notes (ss 489A-489I)`

§§ `s 489A(2) - "bank note", "coin", "currency"`

-- (2) In this section and sections 489B to 489I -
--   "bank note" means a promissory note or engagement for the payment of money
--     to bearer on demand issued by any person carrying on the business of
--     banking in any part of the world, or issued by or under the authority of
--     the government of any country or territory and intended to be used as
--     equivalent to, or as a substitute for, money;
--   "coin" is metal used as money stamped and issued by or under the authority
--     of the government of any country or territory in order to be so used;
--   "currency" includes any currency note or coin (by whatever name called)
--     which is legal tender in the country or territory in which it is issued.
@ref Penal Code 1871 s 489A(2) - the operative atoms
DECLARE `Currency Description Facts` HAS
    `a promissory note or engagement for the payment of money to bearer on demand`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a promissory note or engagement to pay money to bearer on demand?
    `issued by any person carrying on the business of banking in any part of the world`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it issued by a person carrying on the business of banking, anywhere in the world?
    `issued by or under the authority of the government of any country or territory`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it issued by, or under the authority of, the government of any country or territory?
    `intended to be used as equivalent to, or as a substitute for, money`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it intended to be used as equivalent to, or as a substitute for, money?
    `metal used as money`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it metal used as money?
    `stamped and issued by or under the authority of the government of any country or territory in order to be so used`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it stamped and issued by, or under the authority of, the government of a country or territory, to be used as money?
    `a currency note`     IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a currency note, by whatever name called?
    `legal tender in the country or territory in which it is issued`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it legal tender in the country or territory that issued it?

@export Whether a thing is a "bank note" within section 489A(2) of the Penal Code 1871
GIVEN c IS A `Currency Description Facts` @desc The thing, and who issued it
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `bank note within section 489A(2)` c IF
        "'bank note' means"
   ...  c's `a promissory note or engagement for the payment of money to bearer on demand`
   ...  (    c's `issued by any person carrying on the business of banking in any part of the world`
        OR   (    "or"
             ...  c's `issued by or under the authority of the government of any country or territory`
             ...  "and"
             ...  c's `intended to be used as equivalent to, or as a substitute for, money` ) )

@export Whether a thing is a "coin" within section 489A(2) of the Penal Code 1871
GIVEN c IS A `Currency Description Facts` @desc The thing, and who issued it
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `coin within section 489A(2)` c IF
        "'coin' is"
   ...  c's `metal used as money`
   ...  c's `stamped and issued by or under the authority of the government of any country or territory in order to be so used`

@export Whether a thing is "currency" within section 489A(2) of the Penal Code 1871
GIVEN c IS A `Currency Description Facts` @desc The thing, and whether it is legal tender where issued
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `currency within section 489A(2)` c IF
        "'currency' includes any"
   ...  (    c's `a currency note`
        OR   `coin within section 489A(2)` c )
   ...  "(by whatever name called) which is"
   ...  c's `legal tender in the country or territory in which it is issued`

§§ `The facts of a currency offence - ss 489A-489I`

@ref Penal Code 1871 ss 489A-489I - the operative atoms, and the particulars CPC ss 124-125 require
DECLARE `Currency Facts` HAS
    particulars           IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    `the currency`        IS A STRING  @desc The currency, bank notes, coins or instruments, as they are to read after "to wit," - for example "ten counterfeit Singapore $50 currency notes"
    -- the object
    `currency or a bank note`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it currency (a currency note or coin that is legal tender where issued) or a bank note (a bearer note payable on demand issued by a banker or a government), as s 489A(2) defines them?
    `a coin`              IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a coin - metal used as money, stamped and issued by or under the authority of a government to be so used (s 489A(2))?
    `the currency or bank note is forged or counterfeit`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the currency or bank note forged (s 463) or counterfeit (s 28)?
    -- s 489A
    `forges or counterfeits`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 489A: Did the accused forge or counterfeit (s 28) the currency or bank note? (Physical element.)
    `knowingly performs any part of the process of forging or counterfeiting`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 489A: Did the accused knowingly (s 26D) perform any part of the process of forging or counterfeiting it?
    -- s 489B
    `delivers or sells to, or buys or receives from, any other person`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 489B: Did the accused deliver or sell it to, or buy or receive it from, another person? (Physical element.)
    `imports, exports or traffics in`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 489B: Did the accused import, export or traffic in it? (Physical element.)
    `uses as genuine`     IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 489B: Did the accused use it as genuine? (Physical element.)
    `knowing or having reason to believe the same to be forged or counterfeit`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc ss 489B, 489C: Did the accused know, or have reason to believe (s 26), that it was forged or counterfeit? (Fault element.)
    -- ss 489C, 489D, 489I
    `has in his possession`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc ss 489C, 489D, 489I: Did the accused have it in his possession (s 27)? (Physical element.)
    `intending to use the same as genuine or that it may be used as genuine`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc ss 489C, 489I: Did the accused intend to use it as genuine, or that it may be used as genuine? (Fault element.)
    -- s 489D
    `a die, machinery, instrument or material`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 489D: Is the thing a die, machinery, instrument or material?
    `makes, mends or performs any part of the process of making or mending`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 489D: Did the accused make or mend it, or perform any part of the process of making or mending it? (Physical element.)
    `buys, sells or disposes of`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 489D: Did the accused buy, sell or dispose of it? (Physical element.)
    `for the purpose of being used for forging or counterfeiting any currency or bank note`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 489D: Was it for the purpose of being used to forge or counterfeit currency or a bank note?
    `knowing or having reason to believe that it is intended to be used for forging or counterfeiting any currency or bank note`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 489D: Did the accused know, or have reason to believe, that it was intended to be used to forge or counterfeit currency or a bank note? (Fault element.)
    -- s 489E
    `being within Singapore`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 489E: Was the accused within Singapore?
    `abets the counterfeiting of any currency out of Singapore`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 489E: Did the accused abet (s 107 - defined in pc-general-part; joined at integration) the counterfeiting of currency outside Singapore?
    -- s 489F
    fraudulently          IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 489F: Did the accused act fraudulently (s 25)? (Fault element.)
    dishonestly           IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 489F: Did the accused act dishonestly (s 24)? (Fault element.)
    `performs on any coin an operation which diminishes the weight or alters the composition of that coin`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 489F: Did the accused perform on the coin an operation that diminished its weight or altered its composition? Scooping out part of it and putting anything else into the cavity alters its composition (Explanation). (Physical element.)
    -- s 489G
    `performs on any currency an operation which alters the appearance of that currency`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 489G: Did the accused perform on the currency an operation that altered its appearance? (Physical element.)
    `with the intention that that currency will pass as currency of a different description`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 489G: Did the accused intend it to pass as currency of a different description? (Fault element.)
    -- s 489H
    `delivers to any other person as genuine, or as currency of a different description`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 489H: Did the accused deliver it to another person as genuine, or as currency of a different description from what it is? (Physical element.)
    `attempts to induce any person to receive it as genuine, or as currency of a different description`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 489H: Did the accused attempt to induce anyone to receive it as genuine, or as currency of a different description? (Physical element.)
    `knows or has reason to believe that an operation mentioned in section 489F or 489G has been performed on it`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 489H: Did the accused know, or have reason to believe, that an operation of the kind in s 489F (weight or composition of a coin) or s 489G (appearance) had been performed on it? (Fault element.)
    -- s 489I
    `knows or has reason to believe that an offence defined in section 489F or 489G has been committed with respect to it`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 489I: Did the accused know, or have reason to believe, that an offence under s 489F or s 489G had been committed with respect to it? (Fault element.)

§§ `s 489A(1) - forging or counterfeiting currency or bank notes`

-- 489A.-(1) Whoever forges or counterfeits, or knowingly performs any part of
--   the process of forging or counterfeiting, any currency or bank note shall
--   be guilty of an offence and shall on conviction be punished with
--   imprisonment for a term which may extend to 20 years, and shall also be
--   liable to fine.
@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 489A of the Penal Code 1871 (forging or counterfeiting currency or bank notes)
GIVEN f IS A `Currency Facts` @desc The currency, and what the accused did to it
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 489A` f IF
        "(1) Whoever"
   ...  (    f's `forges or counterfeits`
        OR   f's `knowingly performs any part of the process of forging or counterfeiting` )
   ...  "any"
   ...  f's `currency or a bank note`

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 489A(1)
`punishment prescribed by s 489A` MEANS
    `a punishment of imprisonment, and liability to fine` "489A"
        "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 20 years, and shall also be liable to fine" 240

§§ `s 489B - using as genuine forged or counterfeit currency or bank notes`

-- 489B. Whoever delivers or sells to, or buys or receives from, any other
--   person, or otherwise imports, exports or traffics in or uses as genuine,
--   any forged or counterfeit currency or bank note, knowing or having reason
--   to believe the same to be forged or counterfeit, shall be guilty of an
--   offence and shall on conviction be punished with imprisonment for a term
--   which may extend to 20 years, and shall also be liable to fine.
@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 489B of the Penal Code 1871 (using as genuine forged or counterfeit currency or bank notes)
GIVEN f IS A `Currency Facts` @desc The currency, what the accused did with it, and what he knew of it
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 489B` f IF
        "Whoever"
   ...  (    f's `delivers or sells to, or buys or receives from, any other person`
        OR   f's `imports, exports or traffics in`
        OR   f's `uses as genuine` )
   ...  "any forged or counterfeit"
   ...  f's `the currency or bank note is forged or counterfeit`
   ...  f's `currency or a bank note`
   ...  f's `knowing or having reason to believe the same to be forged or counterfeit`

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 489B
`punishment prescribed by s 489B` MEANS
    `a punishment of imprisonment, and liability to fine` "489B"
        "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 20 years, and shall also be liable to fine" 240

§§ `s 489C - possession of forged or counterfeit currency or bank notes`

-- 489C. Whoever has in his possession any forged or counterfeit currency or
--   bank note, knowing or having reason to believe the same to be forged or
--   counterfeit and intending to use the same as genuine or that it may be
--   used as genuine, shall be punished with imprisonment for a term which may
--   extend to 15 years and shall also be liable to fine.
@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 489C of the Penal Code 1871 (possession of forged or counterfeit currency or bank notes)
GIVEN f IS A `Currency Facts` @desc The currency, what the accused knew of it, and what he intended
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 489C` f IF
        "Whoever"
   ...  f's `has in his possession`
   ...  "any forged or counterfeit"
   ...  f's `the currency or bank note is forged or counterfeit`
   ...  f's `currency or a bank note`
   ...  f's `knowing or having reason to believe the same to be forged or counterfeit`
   ...  f's `intending to use the same as genuine or that it may be used as genuine`

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 489C
`punishment prescribed by s 489C` MEANS
    `a punishment of imprisonment, and liability to fine` "489C"
        "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 15 years and shall also be liable to fine" 180

§§ `s 489D - instruments or materials for forging or counterfeiting currency or bank notes`

-- 489D. Whoever makes, mends or performs any part of the process of making or
--   mending or buys, sells or disposes of, or has in his possession, any die,
--   machinery, instrument or material for the purpose of being used, or
--   knowing or having reason to believe that it is intended to be used, for
--   forging or counterfeiting any currency or bank note, shall be punished
--   with imprisonment for a term which may extend to 20 years, and shall also
--   be liable to fine.
@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 489D of the Penal Code 1871 (making or possessing instruments or materials for forging or counterfeiting currency or bank notes)
GIVEN f IS A `Currency Facts` @desc The die, machinery, instrument or material, what the accused did with it, and its purpose
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 489D` f IF
        "Whoever"
   ...  (    f's `makes, mends or performs any part of the process of making or mending`
        OR   f's `buys, sells or disposes of`
        OR   f's `has in his possession` )
   ...  "any"
   ...  f's `a die, machinery, instrument or material`
   ...  (    f's `for the purpose of being used for forging or counterfeiting any currency or bank note`
        OR   f's `knowing or having reason to believe that it is intended to be used for forging or counterfeiting any currency or bank note` )

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 489D
`punishment prescribed by s 489D` MEANS
    `a punishment of imprisonment, and liability to fine` "489D"
        "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 20 years, and shall also be liable to fine" 240

§§ `s 489E - abetting in Singapore counterfeiting of currency out of Singapore`

-- 489E. Whoever, being within Singapore, abets the counterfeiting of any
--   currency out of Singapore, shall be punished in the same manner as if he
--   abetted the counterfeiting of such currency within Singapore.
--
-- The punishment is by reference to abetment (ss 109-117, general-part's) of
-- s 489A; it is carried as the section's words, and the enhanced figures are
-- general-part's to compute (FORK DD-15).
@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 489E of the Penal Code 1871 (abetting in Singapore counterfeiting of currency out of Singapore)
GIVEN f IS A `Currency Facts` @desc Where the accused was, and what he abetted
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 489E` f IF
        "Whoever,"
   ...  f's `being within Singapore`
   ...  f's `abets the counterfeiting of any currency out of Singapore`

§§ `s 489F - diminishing the weight or altering the composition of a coin`

-- 489F. Whoever fraudulently or dishonestly performs on any coin any operation
--   which diminishes the weight or alters the composition of that coin shall
--   be guilty of an offence and shall on conviction be punished with
--   imprisonment for a term which may extend to 7 years, and shall also be
--   liable to fine.
--   Explanation.-A person who scoops out part of the coin and puts anything
--   else into the cavity, alters the composition of that coin.
@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 489F of the Penal Code 1871 (fraudulently or dishonestly diminishing weight or altering composition of any coin)
GIVEN f IS A `Currency Facts` @desc The coin, and what the accused did to it
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 489F` f IF
        "Whoever"
   ...  (    f's fraudulently
        OR   f's dishonestly )
   ...  f's `performs on any coin an operation which diminishes the weight or alters the composition of that coin`
   ...  f's `a coin`

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 489F
`punishment prescribed by s 489F` MEANS
    `a punishment of imprisonment, and liability to fine` "489F"
        "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 7 years, and shall also be liable to fine" 84

§§ `s 489G - altering the appearance of currency`

-- 489G. Whoever performs on any currency any operation which alters the
--   appearance of that currency, with the intention that that currency will
--   pass as currency of a different description, shall be guilty of an
--   offence and shall on conviction be punished with imprisonment for a term
--   which may extend to 7 years, and shall also be liable to fine.
@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 489G of the Penal Code 1871 (altering appearance of currency with intent that it shall pass as currency of different description)
GIVEN f IS A `Currency Facts` @desc The currency, what the accused did to it, and what he intended
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 489G` f IF
        "Whoever"
   ...  f's `performs on any currency an operation which alters the appearance of that currency`
   ...  f's `currency or a bank note`
   ...  f's `with the intention that that currency will pass as currency of a different description`

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 489G
`punishment prescribed by s 489G` MEANS
    `a punishment of imprisonment, and liability to fine` "489G"
        "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 7 years, and shall also be liable to fine" 84

§§ `s 489H - delivery to another of altered currency`

-- 489H. Whoever delivers to any other person as genuine, or as currency of a
--   different description from what it is, or attempts to induce any person to
--   receive as genuine or as a currency of a different description from what
--   it is, any currency in respect of which he knows or has reason to believe
--   that any operation mentioned in section 489F or 489G has been performed,
--   shall be guilty of an offence and shall on conviction be punished with
--   imprisonment for a term which may extend to 10 years, and shall also be
--   liable to fine.
@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 489H of the Penal Code 1871 (delivery to another of altered currency)
GIVEN f IS A `Currency Facts` @desc The currency, what the accused did with it, and what he knew of it
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 489H` f IF
        "Whoever"
   ...  (    f's `delivers to any other person as genuine, or as currency of a different description`
        OR   f's `attempts to induce any person to receive it as genuine, or as currency of a different description` )
   ...  "any"
   ...  f's `currency or a bank note`
   ...  f's `knows or has reason to believe that an operation mentioned in section 489F or 489G has been performed on it`

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 489H
`punishment prescribed by s 489H` MEANS
    `a punishment of imprisonment, and liability to fine` "489H"
        "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 10 years, and shall also be liable to fine" 120

§§ `s 489I - possession of altered currency`

-- 489I. Whoever has in his possession any currency with respect to which he
--   knows or has reason to believe that any offence defined in section 489F or
--   489G has been committed and intending to use such currency as genuine or
--   that it may be used as genuine shall on conviction be punished with
--   imprisonment for a term which may extend to 5 years, and shall also be
--   liable to fine.
@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 489I of the Penal Code 1871 (possession of altered currency)
GIVEN f IS A `Currency Facts` @desc The currency, what the accused knew of it, and what he intended
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 489I` f IF
        "Whoever"
   ...  f's `has in his possession`
   ...  "any"
   ...  f's `currency or a bank note`
   ...  f's `knows or has reason to believe that an offence defined in section 489F or 489G has been committed with respect to it`
   ...  f's `intending to use the same as genuine or that it may be used as genuine`

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 489I
`punishment prescribed by s 489I` MEANS
    `a punishment of imprisonment, and liability to fine` "489I"
        "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 5 years, and shall also be liable to fine" 60

§ `The charges - currency and bank notes`

-- The recitals follow the section's verbs, naming only the limbs that hold.
GIVEN f IS A `Currency Facts`
GIVETH A STRING
`the currency recited` f MEANS
    CONCAT ", to wit, ", f's `the currency`

GIVEN words IS A LIST OF STRING
GIVETH A STRING
`one or more of` words MEANS `joined with` ", or " words

@export Frame a charge under section 489A of the Penal Code 1871 (forging or counterfeiting currency or bank notes), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Currency Facts` @desc The currency, what the accused did to it, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 489A` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "489A" "forging or counterfeiting currency or bank notes"
        (`punishment prescribed by s 489A`'s words)
        (`offence under s 489A` f)
        (CONCAT "did ",
                (`one or more of` (concat (LIST
                    (`included if` (f's `forges or counterfeits`) "forge or counterfeit"),
                    (`included if` (f's `knowingly performs any part of the process of forging or counterfeiting`) "knowingly perform part of the process of forging or counterfeiting")))),
                " currency or bank notes", (`the currency recited` f))
        (concat (LIST
            (`missing unless` (f's `forges or counterfeits` OR f's `knowingly performs any part of the process of forging or counterfeiting`) "forges or counterfeits, or knowingly performs any part of the process of forging or counterfeiting"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `currency or a bank note`) "any currency or bank note")))

@export Frame a charge under section 489B of the Penal Code 1871 (using as genuine forged or counterfeit currency or bank notes), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Currency Facts` @desc The currency, what the accused did with it and knew of it, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 489B` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "489B" "using as genuine forged or counterfeit currency or bank notes"
        (`punishment prescribed by s 489B`'s words)
        (`offence under s 489B` f)
        (CONCAT "did ",
                (`one or more of` (concat (LIST
                    (`included if` (f's `delivers or sells to, or buys or receives from, any other person`) "deliver or sell to, or buy or receive from, another person"),
                    (`included if` (f's `imports, exports or traffics in`) "import, export or traffic in"),
                    (`included if` (f's `uses as genuine`) "use as genuine")))),
                " forged or counterfeit currency or bank notes", (`the currency recited` f),
                ", knowing or having reason to believe the same to be forged or counterfeit")
        (concat (LIST
            (`missing unless` (f's `delivers or sells to, or buys or receives from, any other person` OR f's `imports, exports or traffics in` OR f's `uses as genuine`) "delivers or sells to, or buys or receives from, any other person, or otherwise imports, exports or traffics in or uses as genuine"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `the currency or bank note is forged or counterfeit` AND f's `currency or a bank note`) "any forged or counterfeit currency or bank note"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `knowing or having reason to believe the same to be forged or counterfeit`) "knowing or having reason to believe the same to be forged or counterfeit")))

@export Frame a charge under section 489C of the Penal Code 1871 (possession of forged or counterfeit currency or bank notes), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Currency Facts` @desc The currency, what the accused knew of it and intended, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 489C` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "489C" "possession of forged or counterfeit currency or bank notes"
        (`punishment prescribed by s 489C`'s words)
        (`offence under s 489C` f)
        (CONCAT "did have in your possession forged or counterfeit currency or bank notes", (`the currency recited` f),
                ", knowing or having reason to believe the same to be forged or counterfeit and intending to use the same as genuine or that it may be used as genuine")
        (concat (LIST
            (`missing unless` (f's `has in his possession`) "has in his possession"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `the currency or bank note is forged or counterfeit` AND f's `currency or a bank note`) "any forged or counterfeit currency or bank note"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `knowing or having reason to believe the same to be forged or counterfeit`) "knowing or having reason to believe the same to be forged or counterfeit"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `intending to use the same as genuine or that it may be used as genuine`) "intending to use the same as genuine or that it may be used as genuine")))

@export Frame a charge under section 489D of the Penal Code 1871 (making or possessing instruments or materials for forging or counterfeiting currency or bank notes), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Currency Facts` @desc The die, machinery, instrument or material, what the accused did with it, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 489D` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "489D" "making or possessing instruments or materials for forging or counterfeiting currency or bank notes"
        (`punishment prescribed by s 489D`'s words)
        (`offence under s 489D` f)
        (CONCAT "did ",
                (`one or more of` (concat (LIST
                    (`included if` (f's `makes, mends or performs any part of the process of making or mending`) "make or mend, or perform part of the process of making or mending,"),
                    (`included if` (f's `buys, sells or disposes of`) "buy, sell or dispose of"),
                    (`included if` (f's `has in his possession`) "have in your possession")))),
                " a die, machinery, instrument or material", (`the currency recited` f),
                (IF f's `for the purpose of being used for forging or counterfeiting any currency or bank note`
                 THEN ", for the purpose of being used for forging or counterfeiting currency or bank notes"
                 ELSE ", knowing or having reason to believe that it was intended to be used for forging or counterfeiting currency or bank notes"))
        (concat (LIST
            (`missing unless` (f's `makes, mends or performs any part of the process of making or mending` OR f's `buys, sells or disposes of` OR f's `has in his possession`) "makes, mends or performs any part of the process of making or mending, or buys, sells or disposes of, or has in his possession"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `a die, machinery, instrument or material`) "any die, machinery, instrument or material"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `for the purpose of being used for forging or counterfeiting any currency or bank note` OR f's `knowing or having reason to believe that it is intended to be used for forging or counterfeiting any currency or bank note`) "for the purpose of being used, or knowing or having reason to believe that it is intended to be used, for forging or counterfeiting any currency or bank note")))

@export Frame a charge under section 489E of the Penal Code 1871 (abetting in Singapore counterfeiting of currency out of Singapore), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Currency Facts` @desc Where the accused was, what he abetted, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 489E` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "489E" "abetting in Singapore counterfeiting of currency out of Singapore"
        "in the same manner as if he abetted the counterfeiting of such currency within Singapore"
        (`offence under s 489E` f)
        (CONCAT "being within Singapore, did abet the counterfeiting of currency out of Singapore", (`the currency recited` f))
        (concat (LIST
            (`missing unless` (f's `being within Singapore`) "being within Singapore"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `abets the counterfeiting of any currency out of Singapore`) "abets the counterfeiting of any currency out of Singapore")))

@export Frame a charge under section 489F of the Penal Code 1871 (fraudulently or dishonestly diminishing weight or altering composition of any coin), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Currency Facts` @desc The coin, what the accused did to it, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 489F` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "489F" "fraudulently or dishonestly diminishing weight or altering composition of any coin"
        (`punishment prescribed by s 489F`'s words)
        (`offence under s 489F` f)
        (CONCAT "did ", (`joined with` " and " (concat (LIST (`included if` (f's fraudulently) "fraudulently"), (`included if` (f's dishonestly) "dishonestly")))),
                " perform on a coin an operation which diminished the weight or altered the composition of that coin", (`the currency recited` f))
        (concat (LIST
            (`missing unless` (f's fraudulently OR f's dishonestly) "fraudulently or dishonestly"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `performs on any coin an operation which diminishes the weight or alters the composition of that coin`) "performs on any coin any operation which diminishes the weight or alters the composition of that coin"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `a coin`) "any coin")))

@export Frame a charge under section 489G of the Penal Code 1871 (altering appearance of currency with intent that it shall pass as currency of different description), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Currency Facts` @desc The currency, what the accused did to it and intended, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 489G` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "489G" "altering appearance of currency with intent that it shall pass as currency of different description"
        (`punishment prescribed by s 489G`'s words)
        (`offence under s 489G` f)
        (CONCAT "did perform on currency an operation which altered its appearance", (`the currency recited` f), ", with the intention that that currency would pass as currency of a different description")
        (concat (LIST
            (`missing unless` (f's `performs on any currency an operation which alters the appearance of that currency` AND f's `currency or a bank note`) "performs on any currency any operation which alters the appearance of that currency"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `with the intention that that currency will pass as currency of a different description`) "with the intention that that currency will pass as currency of a different description")))

@export Frame a charge under section 489H of the Penal Code 1871 (delivery to another of altered currency), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Currency Facts` @desc The currency, what the accused did with it and knew of it, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 489H` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "489H" "delivery to another of altered currency"
        (`punishment prescribed by s 489H`'s words)
        (`offence under s 489H` f)
        (CONCAT "did ",
                (IF f's `delivers to any other person as genuine, or as currency of a different description`
                 THEN "deliver to another person as genuine, or as currency of a different description,"
                 ELSE "attempt to induce a person to receive as genuine, or as currency of a different description,"),
                " currency", (`the currency recited` f),
                ", knowing or having reason to believe that an operation mentioned in section 489F or 489G of the Penal Code 1871 had been performed on it")
        (concat (LIST
            (`missing unless` (f's `delivers to any other person as genuine, or as currency of a different description` OR f's `attempts to induce any person to receive it as genuine, or as currency of a different description`) "delivers to any other person, or attempts to induce any person to receive, as genuine or as currency of a different description"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `currency or a bank note`) "any currency"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `knows or has reason to believe that an operation mentioned in section 489F or 489G has been performed on it`) "knows or has reason to believe that any operation mentioned in section 489F or 489G has been performed")))

@export Frame a charge under section 489I of the Penal Code 1871 (possession of altered currency), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Currency Facts` @desc The currency, what the accused knew of it and intended, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 489I` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "489I" "possession of altered currency"
        (`punishment prescribed by s 489I`'s words)
        (`offence under s 489I` f)
        (CONCAT "did have in your possession currency", (`the currency recited` f),
                ", knowing or having reason to believe that an offence defined in section 489F or 489G of the Penal Code 1871 had been committed with respect to it, and intending to use the same as genuine or that it may be used as genuine")
        (concat (LIST
            (`missing unless` (f's `has in his possession`) "has in his possession"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `currency or a bank note`) "any currency"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `knows or has reason to believe that an offence defined in section 489F or 489G has been committed with respect to it`) "knows or has reason to believe that any offence defined in section 489F or 489G has been committed"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `intending to use the same as genuine or that it may be used as genuine`) "intending to use such currency as genuine or that it may be used as genuine")))
